  "title": "Haze4K Frozen-Output Tail-Controller Evidence Review v1",
  "rationale": "The completed tail-controller qualification is scientifically unfavorable on utility and activation but terminally inconclusive because its full reconstruction pass exceeded the frozen 1e-6 identity tolerance. Compact evidence omitted the discrepancy magnitude, location, dtype, file and checkpoint identities, saved-seed consistency, and whether the difference can change the frozen selected actions. This finite receipt-bound review resolves that uncertainty without inference or retraining. It rehashes both cloud workspaces, compares all 600 by 9 saved ensemble utility/risk file pairs, checks current ensembles against their saved three-seed means, and replays the frozen R0_L1 weighted-q/raw/setwise/cap-0.01 actions using upstream frozen tile areas. Scene-level mismatch prevalence supplies formal precision while complete array comparison remains a finite-population census. Raw scene-cell diagnostics remain cloud-only; compact aggregate evidence retains all quantities required for the typed decision.",
  "first_operation": "HAZE4K_FROZEN_OUTPUT_TAIL_CONTROLLER_EVIDENCE_REVIEW",
